falling asleep to the sound of a distant train, and waking up as its conductor.

seeing your worst fear brought to life, standing on its own two feet in front of you, as you meet one another's gaze not with anger or denial or contempt, but simple acknowledgement of the other as an equal.

walking uphill for so long that you've ceased to notice the incline, until you finally turn around and see the view.

a finger held to the lips like the blizzard that blankets city streets into a sweet, fleeting silence.

the first moment of the last bite of the best meal you've ever had.

the silent wish of a paintbrush to be transfigured into an ax breaking open the ice of your soul.

the realization that a lover has slightly misheard something said thirty seconds ago, followed by the abandoning of yourself to the fact that it is too small and to late to correct.

the morning affirmation said by a local water bug before it goes about its day, the name of a great elm tree that lived long ago, and the last words spoken by Krakatoa prior to its 1883 eruption.
